# Python bytecode caches — never commit these. The test suite's "forbidden model
# family" guard scans repo files, and CPython constant-folds that test's split-string
# needle into a single literal inside the compiled .pyc; committing bytecode would leak
# the term and trip a plain `grep -ri` for it over the repo.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
